If `pairs[i].value` is a uint, `cbor_array_size(pairs[i].value)` is called on a non-array item. This could cause issues. But more importantly, if `pairs[i].value` is a uint, `entity->roles[entity_role_cnt++] = role;` is executed without checking if `entity_role_cnt` is within bounds. The `roles` array has 6 elements (`FuCoswidEntityRole roles[6]`). If there are more than 6 uint roles, this would be a stack-buffer-overflow, not heap.

