```

The `cbor_array_get(item, 0)` and `cbor_array_get(item, 1)` are called on `item`. If `item` is not an array, this could be a problem. But in the call chain from `fu_coswid_firmware_parse_file`, `item` is either:
1. `pairs[i].value` which is checked to be an array (in the else branch)
2. An element from `fu_coswid_firmware_parse_hash_array`, which iterates over elements of an array - these elements could be anything

So the vulnerability is in case 2: if an element of the hash array is not itself an array, then `cbor_array_get(item, 0)` on a non-array item could cause a heap-buffer-overflow.

